Package: EMLMLasso
Title: EM Algorithm for Lasso-Penalized Linear Mixed Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Fernanda", "Lang Schumacher", email = "fernandalschumacher@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Daniela C.R.", "Oliveira", role = "aut"),
    person("Victor H.", "Lachos", role = "aut"),
    person("Marcos Santos", "de Oliveira", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits linear mixed models with a lasso penalty on the fixed-effects
    coefficients via an Expectation-Maximization (EM) algorithm. Random effects are
    integrated out at each E-step and the fixed-effects update is solved with a
    coordinate-descent lasso ('glmnet'), so the same penalized-likelihood machinery
    used for ordinary linear models extends naturally to clustered/longitudinal data.
    'EMLasso_BIC_Search()' fits the model over a data-driven grid of penalty values
    and selects the tuning parameter by Bayesian Information Criterion, avoiding the
    heavier cross-validation loop of earlier implementations. Methods described in
    Oliveira, Schumacher, and Lachos (2026) <doi:10.1177/09622802251399913>.
